  "summary": "Distinctive wooden architecture style characteristic of Latvia's seaside resort town of Jurmala.",
  "description": "This architectural style features elaborate wooden structures with decorative elements, steep roofs, and verandas that blend Nordic and Baltic influences. The style developed as Jurmala became a popular resort destination in the late 19th century, with buildings designed to harmonize with the natural environment while providing comfortable summer residences.",
